HubCli
======

HubCli is a fork of OpenCode (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode),
licensed under the MIT License. The original OpenCode copyright and license
text is preserved unmodified in LICENSE.

HubCli is an independent, community-maintained fork. It adds model
curation, diagnostics (`hubcli doctor`), fork-maintenance tooling
(`hubcli maintenance`), routing profiles, and a read-only MCP server on top
of the unmodified OpenCode core. All HubCli-specific behavior is inactive
unless the HUBCLI_BRAND environment variable is set — without it, this
software behaves as unmodified OpenCode.

HubCli is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or an official product of:
  - the OpenCode project or its maintainers,
  - OpenAI,
  - Anthropic,
  - NVIDIA,
  - Alibaba Cloud / DashScope,
  - DeepSeek,
  - or any other model provider it integrates with.

Product and provider names referenced (GPT, Claude, Kimi, MiniMax, Qwen,
GLM, DeepSeek, etc.) are used solely to identify the models HubCli can
route to via each provider's own API, under the user's own credentials.
No trademark rights are claimed.

